# Testing Expectations

- Add or update tests when changing business logic, repositories, or view models.
- Keep tests aligned with the risk and blast radius of the change.
- Favor focused unit tests over broad, fragile coverage.

# Coverage Priorities

- Use cases
- repository behavior
- mapping logic when non-trivial
- view model state transitions

# Test Style

- Keep tests readable and intention-revealing.
- Assert observable behavior, not incidental implementation details.
- Prefer fixtures and mocks already present in the repo over ad hoc setup.

# Review Gate

- If a change touches shared behavior and has no meaningful validation, call that out explicitly.
